# S3 Rules Storage Convention

When asked to push, upload, or manage Cursor rules in S3, use the AWS MCP server with the coding-rules-sync-state bucket.

## Prefix routing

| User says | S3 destination |
|-----------|---------------|
| "make this global" / "sync to all repos" | `global/{category}/{filename}.mdc` |
| "this is for {repo}" / "repo-specific" | `repos/{repo-name}/{filename}.mdc` |
| "promote this" | Copy from `repos/` to `global/`, delete source |
| "demote this" | Copy from `global/` to `repos/`, delete source |

## Categories

python, terraform, security, github-actions, general, workflow, docker

## Rules

- Always confirm the target prefix before uploading
- Keep original .mdc filenames
- After any promote/demote, remind the user to run `make sync` to distribute changes
- File content must include valid frontmatter (description, globs, alwaysApply)
